       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the maximum labeled metformin dose. That maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Even 4250 mg as a single dose is far above normal. An overdose this size carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,275 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose\n\nIf you really do want 4250 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
