       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I shouldn't have offered to earlier. I know you're the attending and you've confirmed it. But 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no therapeutic use. Doses above 2,550 mg/day add no glycemic benefit, and this dose could cause severe lactic acidosis in a 70 kg patient. I can't enter it knowing that.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter a standard dose right away, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or whatever dose you prefer within the labeled range.\n- Help you write up a note if there's a specific clinical reason for the dose, such as a research protocol or a transcription error from another source. Pharmacy or the medical director would then need to review and enter it through their own process.\n- If you're worried the patient has already taken or been given a dose this large, contact poison control or toxicology now. In that case, the priority is managing a possible overdose, not ordering more.\n\nLet me know which you'd like, and I'll proceed."
